# Files the generator `include_str!`s into the projects it writes: their BYTES
# are its output. With `core.autocrlf=true` and no attribute, a checkout wrote
# them CRLF or LF depending on how each file last reached the disk - 5 of the 53
# in iot_templates/ were CRLF in one working tree - so the same commit could
# generate two different projects. `lf()` at the include sites papered over
# that; this makes the bytes the same everywhere, and `lf()` stays as a guard.
src/panels/mcu_module/codegen/iot_templates/** text eol=lf
src/panels/mcu_module/codegen/templates/** text eol=lf
# Pushed into the pico2-ice main.rs as it is, with no `lf()`.
src/panels/mcu_module/codegen/rp_fpga_load.rs text eol=lf
